Revers Of an Array:-

# in case of odd length of list
l=[1,2,3,4,5]
n=len(l)
a=[]
for i in range(n-1, -1, -1): # l to a
    a.append(l[i])
l=[]
for i in range(0,n,1): # a to l
    l.append(a[i])
print(l) 
Output:
[5,4,3,2,1]

Time Complexity: O(n+n) = O(2n) = O(n)
Space Complexity:O(1)


#in case of even length of list
l=[1,2,3,4,5,6]
n=len(l)
start=0
end=n-1
while start<end:
        temp=l[start]
        l[start]=l[end]
        l[end]=temp
        start=start+1
        end=end-1
print(l)
Output:-[6,5,4,3,2,1]

Time Complexity:O(n/2) = O(1/2 n) = O(n)
Space Complexity:O(1)
    
